    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the tip. i looked under the leaves but i'm not seeing any actual bugs, just those little holes and maybe some tiny bits of debris. i checked the soil too and it seems fine. is it possible something is hiding during the day or just coming in at night to do the damage? it's driving me crazy because i can't find the source of it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's certainly possible that the pests are nocturnal, like some types of cutworms or certain beetles, which would make them harder to spot during the day. Those tiny bits of debris could be their droppings, which are often overlooked when you're focused on the holes. You might need to set up a small, temporary trap, perhaps a sticky trap, near the affected plants to catch whatever is causing the damage.\n\nThis is a tricky situation, and sometimes it's just a minor infestation that becomes a bigger problem if left unchecked. Keep an eye out for signs of feeding damage on the stems as well, as some pests prefer to chew near the base. If you can't find the source, try an insecticidal soap spray, which can help knock down pests even if you can't see them clearly.",
